      "body": "## Summary\n\n`VocabParallelEmbedding.get_masked_input_and_mask` is decorated with `@torch.compile(dynamic=True, backend=get_compiler_backend(), disable=_is_npu)` — this guards against NPU but not XPU.\n\ntorch.compile/Inductor codegen on Intel XPU under tensor parallelism is unreliable for this function, causing either:\n- a scheduler watchdog timeout (stuck in Inductor's compile-worker subprocess, see `torch/_inductor/compile_worker/subproc_pool.py` in the thread dump), or\n- a hard crash directly inside the compiled function: `RuntimeError: level_zero backend failed with error: 40 (UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES)`\n\nThis affects any TP>1 vision model that routes position-embedding lookups through `VocabParallelEmbedding` on `intel_xpu`, observed on `meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B` (TP4) and `internlm/Intern-S2-Preview` (TP8) — both crash/hang inside `get_masked_input_and_mask` via `VocabParallelEmbedding.forward` → `_embed_local_shard`.\n\n`sglang/srt/speculative/spec_utils.py` already guards the identical pattern with `disable=_is_npu or _is_xpu`; this applies the same guard here.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `_is_xpu = is_xpu()` and change the decorator to `disable=_is_npu or _is_xpu`.\n\n## Test plan\n\nValidated on real XPU hardware (4x Intel Arc Pro B60, TP4) against the exact `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-xpu` release image running `meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B`:\n\n- Before fix: crashes inside `get_masked_input_and_mask` (via `muse_glimmer.py` vision tower → `position_embedding_table`) on the very first vision-embedding lookup, every run.\n- After fix: the crash no longer occurs at that call site, confirmed across multiple runs — the model proceeds past vision embedding into decode.\n\nNote: on this specific 24GB-per-card hardware at TP4, a separate, pre-existing `mem_fraction_static` headroom issue (unrelated to this fix) can still surface a `UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES` later during decode at the default 0.85 static KV-cache fraction — confirmed independent of this change and resolved by lowering `--mem-fraction-static`. That is a deployment-config tuning issue, not an sglang code bug, and is being tracked separately.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38241024672](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38241024672)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38241024041](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38241024041)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38241024155](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38241024155)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
